@0    = ~If it's dancing you want, I'm good with that. I mean, I don't know a lot of the steps, but I'm fast on my feet.~
@1    = ~Poetry, though...can't get my head around it.~
@2    = ~What are you talking about, Faren?~
@3    = ~I like you just the way you are, Faren. Don't change for me.~
@4    = ~There's no need to get jealous, Faren. Solaufein and I were just enjoying a moment.~
@5    = ~That drow. He's quite taken with you, isn't he?~
@6    = ~It's true - and I am taken with him, too.~
@7    = ~I much prefer your company to his. You have nothing to worry about.~
@8    = ~Heh, good to know. On the other hand...~
@9    = ~He seemed to be enjoying it a little too much, if you ask me.~
@10   = ~Okay. Fair enough, then.~
@11   = ~But - after all that's happened? I didn't--~
@12   = ~Fine. You know what? If you want that melancholy bastard, you're welcome to him.~
@13   = ~Heh, good to know. Thanks.~
@14   = ~You strike me as the sort who prefers levity to serious matters. Why do you suppose that is?~
@15   = ~Wouldn't say I'm either way or the other, really. I mean, I don't go out of my way to make myself miserable, if that's what you're asking.~
@16   = ~It must indeed be an uncomplicated life.~
@17   = ~Oh, yeah? You try living in my shoes, and then we'll talk about uncomplicated.~
@18   = ~Oh, yeah? You try stepping out with a Bhaalspawn with nightmares that make your teeth rattle. Then we'll talk about uncomplicated.~
@19   = ~Do you read, Faren?~
@20   = ~What - for fun, you mean?~
@21   = ~For fun, for education - take it as you will.~
@22   = ~I like Korinna Hazelworth. She writes these pamphlets about - uh, well, they might not quite be your kind of thing...~
@23   = ~Some ribald tale?~
@24   = ~No, not so much. Just that they're all about fighting tentacled things in the Underdark, and, well, your people don't come out in them too well.~
@25   = ~Ah.~
@26   = ~But apart from that, they're really good!~
@27   = ~I always wanted to learn how to do magic for combat. I can't imagine how you keep concentrating like that.~
@28   = ~For the Drow, it is mandatory. I wonder whether I would have this aptitude were it not for my upbringing in Ust Natha.~
@29   = ~I was just trying to give you a compliment, Solaufein. No need to turn it into a lecture.~
@30   = ~I merely think aloud. You may listen, or not, as you please.~
@31   = ~But I thank you for your words.~
